      "id": "hdpfibf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background of Fundamental Duties"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Fundamental Duties were incorporated into Part IV-A and Article 51A of the Indian Constitution upon the recommendation of the Swaran Singh Committee.",
        "The 42nd Constitutional Amendment Act of 1976 originally added 10 Fundamental Duties for Indian citizens.",
        "The 11th Fundamental Duty, making education mandatory for children aged 6 to 14, was added by the 86th Constitutional Amendment Act in 2002.",
        "Fundamental Duties serve as a constant reminder to citizens of their obligations while enjoying their Fundamental Rights.",
        "Like Directive Principles, Fundamental Duties are non-justiciable and cannot be directly enforced in courts without specific legislative enactments."
      ],
      "id": "rj2arch"
    },
